# DTV prototypes

Pages are 1280×720 compositions. Do not invent chrome.

Before writing a screen, answer: **level** (1 / 2 / 3), **menu** (configured / hint trail / hidden / off), **rail** (left or right, never both), **overlay** (named from the chrome footprint), **focus** and **back**.

## Where to write

- Scratch: `apps/storybook/stories/Playground/` — duplicate `Starter.stories.tsx`
- Product: promote to `apps/storybook/stories/Pages/` when it passes [Guidelines/Navigation](apps/storybook/stories/Guidelines/Navigation.mdx)
- Never add prototype screens or new chrome to `packages/react`

## Clone a template

| Level | Start from |
| --- | --- |
| 1 Home | `Templates/Home` or Playground `Starter` |
| 2 focused trail | `Templates/FocusedRail` |
| 3 tall card / VOD | `Templates/SingleInteractivity` |

Keep `TvFrame`, `Overlay`, `HomeMenu`, `TopShelf` / `ContentTrail`. Fill slots with `@dtv/react` (`MainButton`, `MenuItem`, `RoundButton`).

## Overlay

Use an existing variant (`home`, `homeButtonsStart`, `homeButtonsEnd`, `interactivityCardsStart`, `interactivityCardsEnd`, …). Do not invent a new stack per page.

## Data

Map API/fixture payloads into `ShelfCard` / menu props (`Pages/home/mapEpg.ts`, `mapWeather.ts`). Do not hardcode copy on `MainButton`. Do not fetch from `@dtv/react`.

## Don’t

- Skip Level 2 to open an interactivity from Home
- Keep the main menu visible on Level 2
- Mix left and right rails on the same page
- Treat VOD as a fourth level
- Spawn a hint trail from the Globo bug
- Put primary actions top-right except the bug (L1) or Close (L3)
